      "inputText": "Hello everyone.\nLast year I self-published a book about an attempt I made to get really good at playing table tennis.\nIt did 'well' in that it topped some of the Amazon best-seller lists and remained near the top for the rest of the year. It's currently still #1 on the USA Amazon kindle table tennis bestseller list.\nBut despite that sales haven't been great.\nIn the last year it has sold:\nPaperback: 443 copies sold - £1,665.39 (~$2,200)\nKindle: 429 copies sold - £1,003.46 (~$1,400)\nAudiobook: 82 copies sold - £405.57 (~$550)\nTo be honest, I thought there would be a lot more demand. I got pretty excited when I saw the best-seller tag and soon deflated after checking the sales figures.\nTo the more experienced writers, how does this compare with your experiences?\nIf you're interested in a more detailed breakdown of how the year went you can check out my post on it.\n",
